                  "fill": "$color-feedback-warning",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Three rulings specific to money",
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "GQDSp",
                  "name": "Body",
                  "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A failed money operation never gets a toast. It gets a persistent surface carrying the retry, because a transient message can be missed and the user is left believing money moved.  ·  Anything that moves, deletes or reclassifies money is a consequential submission under SC 3.3.4: review-and-confirm naming the record and the amount, or a reversal with a stated window.  ·  Optimistic UI is allowed for categorisation and renaming, never for a transfer. The rule is whether being wrong for two seconds is recoverable by the user alone.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
