                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants are rows, interaction states are columns, so the rest column is the variant showcase and nothing is drawn twice. Hover and active are fill shifts; focus is the ring, drawn outside the control and additive to whatever fill is underneath. Disabled keeps its label readable — it is exempt from the contrast minimum, not from being understandable — and stays focusable so a keyboard user can discover why it is off.",
