                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wD9t5",
                  "name": "Contract",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Three states per row so each specimen keeps a realistic width. Rest state uses border-strong so the control clears 3:1 non-text contrast unaided. The focus ring sits outside the control, radius = control radius + ring padding. Placeholder text uses color-text-placeholder at 6.2:1 — a placeholder is live content, not an inactive control, so the WCAG contrast exemption does not cover it. The value never wraps; the field clips and scrolls. Affix cells, the error message and the label all live outside this atom: the first as a configuration, the last two in the Form field molecule.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": "$type-size-body-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
