            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "eDQx3",
              "name": "What the matrix decides",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$color-bg-subtle",
              "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 7,
              "padding": [
                14,
                16
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "vqgNE",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "What the matrix decides",
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "k5LlJ",
                  "name": "Error leaves the chrome alone",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 2,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "BEw1T",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Error leaves the chrome alone",
                      "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "nRGfa",
                      "name": "B",
                      "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The border and the message carry the error; the affix keeps its neutral treatment. Tinting the currency cell red claims the currency is what is wrong, when the problem is the value beside it.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "kHcEf",
                  "name": "Disabled dims everything, including the chrome",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 2,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "pGjuX",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Disabled dims everything, including the chrome",
                      "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "dQ0Sw",
                      "name": "B",
                      "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Symbol, icon and value all drop to the disabled tone together. An affix that stays crisp beside a dimmed value reads as still-editable.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "r5qjc",
                  "name": "Read-only removes the border, so the affix needs a divider",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 2,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "V3Q6ij",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The affix recedes toward the canvas in both themes",
                      "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "fCiSb",
                      "name": "B",
                      "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The affix cell is tinted with color-bg-affix, which sits between the canvas and the field surface in both themes — darker than the field in light, darker than the field in dark. An earlier version reused color-bg-subtle, which is lighter than the surface in dark, so the affix advanced instead of receding and read as a raised block. Contrast ratios are the wrong tool for judging this: they measure text legibility, and two large adjacent surfaces separate at ratios far below any text threshold — zebra rows work at about 1.05:1. What matters is the direction of the step, not its size.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "TFtyP",
                  "name": "Exclusion",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A leading icon and a currency affix never appear together — same edge, and a search field and an amount field are not the same control.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "unHRN",
              "name": "Precedence",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$color-feedback-info-bg",
              "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 6,
              "padding": [
                14,
                16
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "mZMpE",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$color-feedback-info",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Precedence when more than one applies",
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "z22Mz",
                  "name": "Order",
                  "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "disabled  →  read-only  →  error  →  focus  →  hover  →  rest",
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "LgZv3",
                  "name": "Body",
                  "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The leftmost applicable state owns the control's fill and border. Focus is the exception that stacks rather than replaces: the ring is drawn on top of whatever treatment won, which is why a disabled control can still show it. The message row is independent of all of this — it renders the error wording whenever an error exists, even under a disabled control.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "j3mNr",
          "name": "Selection controls",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
