                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Label, control, and exactly one message. The message row is always present — a hint at rest, an error when invalid — so validation never reflows the form beneath it. The label is always visible: a placeholder is not a label, because it disappears the moment someone starts typing. The error names the fix, is announced in code, and carries an icon, so it never depends on the red alone. The focus ring lives on a wrapper, not on the control, which is why focus costs no layout shift — and why the wrapper can hold any control, a text input or an amount field alike.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": "$type-size-body-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
